        "language": "english",
        "review": "This game has the foundations of a great game, but it's not there yet.\n\nAt its core, it has the potential to become something great.\nThe combat is fluid and fun, and the enemies and boss mechanics are fun to fight.\n\nBut, the game is ridiculously short and empty. This game has maybe 2 hours of content before there's not much more to do.\n\nThe runs are mostly the same every time. The buffs are unimpressive, and there's not much variety. The runs are so short, by the time you get a build going, the game is over.\n\nThe story consists of doing boring, meaningless objectives. This wouldn't be so bad if the runs didn't get so repetitive so quickly.\n\nI hope they continue to develop the game into what it can be, but for now, it's not close to worth the $28 price.\n\nIf you can get it for ~$10, go for it, but it's not worth full price.",
